ies in the world, citizenship in Vatican City isn’t solely provided to people that are born in the country. As there are no hospitals in the Vatican State, virtually no one is born in there. Instead, Vatican citizenship is provided on a ‘jus officii’ basis.","ref":"2019 October 3, Ellen Curtin, “Everything You Wanted to Know about Vatican City”, in City Wonders, archived from the original on 13 Jun 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[57,64],[165,172],[224,231]],"id":"1fffb0fd-9e3c-4acf-bacd-b7e34c023151"}],"links":[["Vatican City","Vatican City"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Relating to the Vatican City state."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"4d3ca771-0b17-47ce-a21e-2c3d26c373cd"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"VAT":{"id":"2749e101-e33f-4f21-9c47-4fd4c6fea5d9","word":"VAT","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"initialism for value-added tax — see also value added tax","word":"IVA"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"And neither party is up for imposing a VAT in place of the current income tax system.","ref":"2024 December 28, Jonathan Nicholson, “Yes, There Are Ways To Cut The Budget Deficit. 'DOGE' Hasn’t Found Them So Far.”, in HuffPost:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[39,42]],"id":"1b1532f1-8c19-4d6f-a53e-1f56449240f9"}],"topics":["economics","government","sciences","taxation"],"wikidata":["Q128635"],"senseid":["en:Q128635"],"categories":["English initialisms","English terms with quotations","en:Taxation"],"links":[["taxation","taxation"],["value added tax","value added tax#English:_Q128635"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"GST"}],"raw_glosses":["(taxation) Initialism of value added tax."],"glosses":["Initialism of value added tax."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism","uncountable"],"alt_of":[{"word":"value added tax"}],"id":"47be49a6-65dc-469b-b041-3e648243e993"},{"categories":["English initialisms"],"links":[["vigilance","vigilance#English"],["awareness","a